      "role": "user",
      "content": "those are okay, but they're still a bit too... \"textbook.\" they sound like a sports science journal. \n\ni want something that feels more like a description of a nuisance. you know, that feeling when everything is going fine and then suddenly this tiny, nagging, almost malicious force just rolls in and ruins the whole set? it's like there are these little, unseen things that just thrive on sabotaging your focus and your energy right when you need it most. \n\ncan you give me some more options that capture that specific feeling? like, the feeling of being picked at or sabotaged by these small, annoying, almost \"mischievous\" sources of exhaustion or distraction that you can't quite pin down? i want it to feel like i'm dealing with these persistent, little pests that keep trying to steal my progress.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
